# No em dashes or AI punctuation

Do not use decorative or "AI-looking" characters in **any** project text: UI copy, i18n JSON, seed content, comments, docs, commits, or PR descriptions.

## Banned

| Character | Name | Use instead |
|---|---|---|
| `—` | Em dash | Comma, period, colon, or parentheses |
| `–` | En dash (as punctuation) | Hyphen `-` for ranges/compounds, or rephrase |
| `…` | Ellipsis character | Three ASCII dots `...` |
| `“` `”` `‘` `’` | Curly quotes / apostrophes | Straight `"` and `'` |
| `•` `●` `★` `✦` and similar | Decorative bullets / stars | `-` lists or plain words |
| `→` `←` `⇒` as prose | Arrow ornaments | ASCII `->` / `<-` only when needed in code/docs tables |

## Allowed

- Normal ASCII hyphen `-` in code, flags, and compound words (`Parthian-Sasanian`)
- Persian/Arabic letters and ZWNJ (`‌`) in FA/AR copy
- Math/code operators that are not decorative prose

## Examples

```text
Bad:  Changing the slug breaks old QR codes — reprint plaques.
Good: Changing the slug breaks old QR codes. Reprint plaques.

Bad:  Loading…
Good: Loading...

Bad:  the site’s page
Good: the site's page
```

Empty UI placeholders: use ASCII `-`, not `—`.
